<title>FRANCE: French tax shortfall 15-17 bln Ffr - Sautter.</title>
<headline>French tax shortfall 15-17 bln Ffr - Sautter.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's tax shortfall for 1997 is running at 15 to 17 billion francs, Budget Minister Christian Sautter said on Monday, detailing the findings of an audit of the public finances.</p>
<p>He told a news conference that the spending overshoot was between 12 and 20 billion francs.</p>
</text>
